Make the whole-frame effects agree across a tiled window.
Co-created with DeepSeek, 2026-11-13. See NOTICE for project terms.

0054 gave the film canvas a window. This makes the effects that were still
whole-frame-only work in that window:

* The date back. Its group is already placed in whole-frame millimetres; the
  window clips it and offsets the mask. The date on a bare frame (no film
  edge) gets the same treatment through an identity layout over the full
  frame, so a tiled export can carry a date with or without the edge.

* Grain and the glare/micro-structure fields. Their values are drawn from a
  per-pixel RNG; the draw is now indexed by the *whole frame's* pixel (first
  pixel, row stride delta and window width travel in the kernel meta), so a
  window is a crop of the one realisation. All-zero on the whole-frame path,
  which is therefore bit-identical.

* The window itself no longer requires the film edge: with grain, glare or a
  date it is what keeps their coordinates global, and set_source_shape still
  takes the pitch from the full frame.

The film-edge date no longer refuses a windowed render. Halation has a wide
3-sigma at its maximum strength, so the host's overlap grows to 192 px when it
is on; the engine needs no new radius plumbing for that.
